I have written a simple C program (nph-canimation) to allow for the
quick and simple animation of images on web pages utilising the
netscape x-mixed-replace html extension.

You can get the program (version 1) and read more about it at:
        <URL:http://www.pipex-sa.net/~nic/animation/>

The features of the program include:

        1) The program reads its input from a text file which you
           specify when calling it. So the same program can be
           used for may different animation sequences.
        2) From the command line, you can specify a delay time
           to delay between each image.
        3) From the command line, you can specify a repeat count,
           to cause the animation to repeat the number of times
           you want.
        4) Various display tions can be specified on the command
           line to modify the way the images are displayed. The
           currently available options are:
                NORMAL MODE - images are displayed
                NORMAL MODE - images are displayed
                                     in the order they appear in filelist.
                INVERTED MODE - images are displayed
                                     in the reverse order of how they appear
                                     in filelist i.e., the last image listed is
                                     displayed first and first image listed
                                     is displayed last.
                RANDOM MODE - images are displayed in a
                                     random order with no guarantee that all
                                     images will be displayed in one repeat
                                     cycle.
                ALL RANDOM MODE - images are displayed
                                     in a random order, but ALL images are
                                     displayed in a repeat cycle with each
                                     image being displayed only once.
                SINGLE RANDOM MODE - images are displayed
                                     in a random order with no guarantee that
                                     all images will be displayed in one repeat
                                     cycle. However, the same image IS NEVER
                                     displayed twice in a row.
                PROGRAM PICK - the program randomly
                                   selects one of the valid display
                                   options.
                UP/DOWN - images are displayed in order and then in the
                                    reverse order
                RANDOM START MODE - begin displaying images from a randomly
                                    selected point in filelist until the
                                    end of the image lsit is reached.
                                    Then, display images from top of the list
                                    until the starting point is reached.


        5) The C source and compilied versions for Linux (gcc version 2.7.3)
           and Solaris 2.4 (gcc version 2.7.0) are available.

Please check this program out and try it out. I would greatly
appreciate all feedback, good or bad.

